{"id": "EUVD-2026-97611", "enisaUuid": "77a71079-7931-329d-850f-9baaadd1ca24", "description": "SiYuan v3.7.0 before v3.8.6 contains an absolute path traversal vulnerability in the kernel's private plugin HTTP server, which passes a kernel plugin handler's ResponseFile.Path to gin's Context.File without validation. Attackers supplying a malicious kernel plugin can return an absolute path to read any file readable by the SiYuan process, including the API token and conf.json.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:05:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:54:55", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/siyuan-note/siyuan/security/advisories/GHSA-phmw-4rgv-r4xv", "https://github.com/siyuan-note/siyuan/commit/c6494375ea40ee973f430f0e85d50f1862a30d81", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/siyuan-3.7.0-before-3.8.6-arbitrary-file-read-via-plugin-responsefile-path"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109309", "GHSA-g3cr-c99q-2hfc"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.38, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6c75bbdb-8161-3433-a72a-6bff24c6ba29", "product": {"name": "SiYuan", "vendor": {"name": "siyuan-note"}}, "product_version": "3.7.0 <3.8.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ec680552-0be3-35c1-99ea-9ec58bb0078a", "vendor": {"name": "siyuan-note"}}], "isExploited": false}